<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Copper Scroll project sites 2026-11-11</name>
<Placemark><name>Tell es-Sultan</name><description>Status: Checked. tell. Position: image, tile F017b (1 Dec 1974) (error approximately 50 m). Ancient Jericho. Mound approximately 270 by 150 m. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0116641 (6 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.4443,31.871,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tulul Abu el-ʿAlayiq, southern mound</name><description>Status: Checked. palace complex. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 50 m). Plan test with Netzer 1975 fig. 2; sunken garden wall, pool B107. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0117120 (56 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.4367,31.8506,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Birket Musa</name><description>Status: Checked. pool. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 50 m). 174 by 143 m on the image; Survey 172 by 144 m. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0117122 (37 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.4402,31.8479,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Quruntul, summit enclosure</name><description>Status: Checked. enclosure (modern wall). Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 80 m). Modern wall with the unfinished church; not the ancient fort (Meshel 1978). EAMENA record: EAMENA-0117189 (148 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.4289,31.8746,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Nebi Musa</name><description>Status: Checked (plan test). shrine compound. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 60 m). Ground plan by V. Pirsky (Daʿadli 2020, fig. 9) agrees with the image of 1 Dec 1974 with scale from its bar, north from its arrow and one anchor (north-east corner): outer walls, inner court and south range to 3 to 6 m. No EAMENA record within 400 m. Checklist record sit0057</description><Point><coordinates>35.4317,31.7867,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Deir Hajla</name><description>Status: Checked. monastery. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 50 m). Position, size and layout; compound 40 by 70 m in 1974. Same form on 5 May 1978: south block 39 by 37 m with dome mark, north court 26 by 34 m. Dark spot at this place on CORONA 26 Sep 1967. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0117124 (30 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.5014,31.82,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Khirbet Qumran</name><description>Status: Checked. settlement. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 60 m). Plan test with Magen and Peleg 2007 fig. 4. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0117926 (76 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.4598,31.741,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>ʿEin Feshkha building</name><description>Status: Checked. building. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 60 m). Plan tests with Humbert and Chambon pl. XLIII and Hirschfeld 2004 fig. 3. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0117992 (91 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.4525,31.7159,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hyrcania (Khirbet el-Mird)</name><description>Status: Checked. fort with reservoirs and aqueducts. Position: image, tile F018b; summit of the elevation model 28 m (error approximately 50 m). Reservoirs and fort Checked with plans of Wright and Patrich; aqueduct course mostly not identified. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0117997 (33 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.3659,31.7192,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mar Saba</name><description>Status: Checked. monastery. Position: image, tile F018b (error approximately 50 m). Position only</description><Point><coordinates>35.3314,31.7051,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Khirbet Mazin</name><description>Status: Checked. building at the shore. Position: image, tile F018b (three-point transform with shift) (error approximately 50 m). Compared with the orthophoto of HA 136 (2024)</description><Point><coordinates>35.4429,31.6819,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Plateau Fort</name><description>Status: Checked. fort (Iron Age II). Position: image, tile A015c (25 Jun 1974) (error approximately 60 m). 50.5 by 49.5 m; no cistern recorded. Square outline also on CORONA 26 Sep 1967. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0184448 "Matabi" (117 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.6844,31.8416,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Habbasa</name><description>Status: Checked. fort with five cisterns. Position: image, tile A017e (1 Dec 1974) (error approximately 50 m). Row of roofless chambers, approximately 50 m; plan test with Prag and Barnes fig. 9. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0185957 (70 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.6793,31.8396,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Barakat</name><description>Status: Checked (form); Probable (position). fort. Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 80 m). Grid reference in Prag and Barnes is 340 to 385 m south of this place (probable error in the paper). EAMENA record: EAMENA-0184843 (31.85302 N, 35.67183 E; 144 m west of the fort on the image, at the same latitude)</description><Point><coordinates>35.6733,31.8527,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kafrein dam, centre of the crest</name><description>Status: Checked. dam (built after 26 September 1967). Position: elevation model (error approximately 30 m). Control point; crest 469 m on the image, 480 m published. No dam and no water on CORONA 26 Sep 1967</description><Point><coordinates>35.6761,31.8511,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell Kafrein</name><description>Status: Checked. tell. Position: elevation model; OpenBible point 30 m (error approximately 30 m). Control point. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0186072 (30 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.6526,31.8507,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell el-Hammam, upper tell</name><description>Status: Checked. tell. Position: elevation model (middle of the ridge) (error approximately 50 m). Control point; OpenStreetMap outline agrees. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0185516 (55 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.674,31.8407,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tree group at the foot of Tell el-Hammam</name><description>Status: Seen. probable springs. Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 80 m). Probable place of the warm springs</description><Point><coordinates>35.6719,31.8387,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Umm Ḥadhar hill, dark patch</name><description>Status: Probable (hill). building with well-cistern (literature). Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 100 m). Building Possible on HEXAGON; Checked by form on APAAME frames. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0185896 "tell haddar" (50 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.6754,31.863,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell er-Rameh</name><description>Status: Checked. tell. Position: elevation model = published point; image 45 to 95 m (error approximately 30 m). The round mound beside the straight road. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0185988 (13 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.6443,31.8257,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Oval mound north-east of Tell er-Rameh</name><description>Status: Seen. hill. Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 80 m). Not Tell er-Rameh; no name</description><Point><coordinates>35.6491,31.8299,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell Iktanu</name><description>Status: Checked (position and form). tell. Position: elevation model; OpenBible point 60 m (error approximately 40 m). Light oval hill north-west of the highway. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0185948 (46 m). Fort on the summit: Prag 1989 fig. 6 has it at −130 m (elevation model −128 m); Glueck gave 42 by 35 by 35 by 20 m; the rectangular outline of approximately 45 by 30 m on the image agrees</description><Point><coordinates>35.6713,31.8192,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Dark area east of the highway (fields)</name><description>Status: Seen (not a hill). hill. Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 80 m). Light on CORONA 26 Sep 1967, dark on 25 Jun 1974: plants of one season. Not the south hill of Iktanu</description><Point><coordinates>35.6745,31.8184,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Road works beside the Dead Sea road</name><description>Status: Seen. military works (20th century). Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 80 m). Not ancient</description><Point><coordinates>35.6762,31.8217,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Machaerus, citadel hill</name><description>Status: Checked. fort with cisterns. Position: elevation model summit (image position is 213 m west: relief displacement) (error approximately 30 m). Identified on the image of 1974 before the excavations of 1978 to 1981</description><Point><coordinates>35.6238,31.5675,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell es-Samarat</name><description>Status: Possible (1974); Checked on the frames of 1918. tell. Position: direction and distance from Tell es-Sultan (Survey sheet): 210 degrees, 740 m (error approximately 80 m). Oval area of approximately 60 by 140 m in the fields in 1974</description><Point><coordinates>35.4404,31.8652,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sugar mill (Tawahin es-Sukkar)</name><description>Status: Possible (1974); Checked on the frames of 1918. mill compound. Position: direction and distance from Tell es-Sultan (Survey sheet): 285 degrees, 535 m (error approximately 80 m). Buildings with trees in 1974; old compound not separated from farm buildings</description><Point><coordinates>35.4388,31.8723,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>ʿAin ez-Zara oasis (Callirrhoe)</name><description>Status: Probable. oasis with excavated buildings (literature). Position: image, tile F018b east shore window (centre of the field area) (error approximately 150 m). Farmed plain with spring courses and no shore road in 1974; the excavated buildings are not identified on the image</description><Point><coordinates>35.5637,31.5968,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Canyon mouth with a round fan north of the oasis</name><description>Status: Probable. wadi mouth. Position: image, tile F018b east shore window (error approximately 150 m). Probable mouth of Wadi Zarqa Maʿin</description><Point><coordinates>35.5655,31.62,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jericho palaces, Pools Complex (two pools)</name><description>Status: Checked. two pools with halls. Position: image, tile F007c (5 May 1978) (error approximately 40 m). Plan test with Netzer 2001 plan 14 (scale of the bar, one anchor, turn 13 degrees from the plan north); each pool approximately 18 by 14 m on the image</description><Point><coordinates>35.4345,31.8541,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jericho palaces, northern wing of the third palace</name><description>Status: Checked. palace wing. Position: image, tile F007c (error approximately 40 m). Plan test with Netzer 1975 fig. 2; agreement 10 to 20 m. Second test with Netzer 2001 plan 35 by the site grid; agreement 5 to 10 m</description><Point><coordinates>35.4367,31.8522,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jericho palaces, Twin Palaces (Area AE)</name><description>Status: Checked. excavated buildings. Position: image, tile F007c (error approximately 50 m). Plan test with Netzer 2001 plan 26 by the site grid (no free value; anchor and turn from plan 14); agreement 5 to 10 m on the image of 5 May 1978</description><Point><coordinates>35.4349,31.8533,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jericho palaces, Area AA (Buried Palace and Fortified Palace)</name><description>Status: Probable. palace mound. Position: image, tile F007c (5 May 1978) (error approximately 50 m). Netzer 2001 plan 11 by the site grid; trenches and rooms inside the frame of the plan; agreement 10 to 20 m</description><Point><coordinates>35.4335,31.854,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell Iktanu, lower south hill</name><description>Status: Checked (position and form). hill (settlement in the literature). Position: image and elevation model: middle of the spur (error approximately 50 m). Long flat-topped spur, approximately 600 by 150 m, south-east of the highway, from south-west to north-east. Agrees with the description in Prag 2024 (Introduction) and with EAMENA-0184805 "iktanu south" (31.81589 N, 35.66924 E). Site plan (her Fig. 1.1) not seen. Prag 1989 fig. 1 (contour plan of the south hill): long hill beside the Dead Sea–Amman road, top at −144 m (elevation model −145 m)</description><Point><coordinates>35.6701,31.8166,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jericho palaces, Herod's Second Palace (Areas AG and AL)</name><description>Status: Probable. palace. Position: image, tile F007c (5 May 1978) (error approximately 50 m). Netzer 2001 plan 29 by the site grid; excavated rooms inside the frame of the plan, east of the Twin Palaces</description><Point><coordinates>35.4351,31.8534,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jericho palaces, Area AC</name><description>Status: Probable. excavated buildings. Position: image, tile F007c (error approximately 50 m). Netzer 2001 plan 12 by the site grid; west part of the palace mound</description><Point><coordinates>35.4334,31.8542,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jericho palaces, Hasmonean Garden of the Pools Complex</name><description>Status: Possible. garden enclosure. Position: site grid of Netzer 2001 plan 25 (error approximately 50 m). Open ground north of the pools on the image; no test is possible</description><Point><coordinates>35.4346,31.8546,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell Nimrin</name><description>Status: Checked (plan test). tell. Position: image, tile A017e (1 Dec 1974), window registered to the elevation model (26 blocks, 12 m) (error approximately 50 m). Topographic map of 1989 (Flanagan and McCreery 1990, fig. 4) agrees with scale from its bar, north from its arrow and one anchor: road cut, mound contours and the old school building, to approximately 10 m. Mound approximately 170 by 110 m. EAMENA-0184259 (40 m). Checklist record sit0308</description><Point><coordinates>35.6251,31.901,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Shunat Nimrin, road junction</name><description>Status: Checked. village and road junction. Position: CORONA DF041 d registered to HEXAGON A017e (43 blocks, 11 m) (error approximately 40 m). Same roads and walled compound in 1967 and 1974</description><Point><coordinates>35.6212,31.8997,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Suwwan</name><description>Status: Checked. rubble mound on a spur (possible building). Position: image, tile A017e (1 Dec 1974), Kafrein transform (error approximately 60 m). Dark speckled patch approximately 25 by 30 m on a spur top between two gullies. Agrees in size and ground form with 17 APAAME photographs of 28 Oct 2014 (title Suwwan; Flickr list position 231 m away). CORONA 1967 too light. No straight sides visible. No EAMENA record within 500 m Second image: HEXAGON A014c of June 1974, registered to the elevation model (25 blocks, 30 m), shows a group of dark spots at the east end of the same gully, at the same place to approximately 30 m. Checked for the presence of the stone patch on two images; no building form is visible.</description><Point><coordinates>35.6875,31.8746,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Karama Ruin 5 (Ain al-Heri)</name><description>Status: Checked. building of two parts on a spur. Position: image, tile A017e (1 Dec 1974), window registered to the elevation model (155 blocks, 12 m) (error approximately 30 m). Two joined rectangles with dark wall lines, approximately 22 by 36 m and 36 by 24 m, on a flat spur top above a gorge with vegetation. Same form on APAAME photographs of 24 Sep 2017 (title Karama Ruin 5 / Heri / Ain al-Heri; Flickr list position 137 m away). No EAMENA record within 500 m Second image: HEXAGON A015c of June 1974 shows the same two joined rectangles.</description><Point><coordinates>35.6666,31.7689,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>el-Heri Tower</name><description>Status: Checked. round stone structure. Position: image, tile A017e (1 Dec 1974), window registered to the elevation model (155 blocks, 12 m) (error approximately 30 m). One oval ring approximately 10 m across on open ground south of a small wadi. APAAME photographs of 24 Sep 2017 show a small round stone structure on a plateau (Flickr list position 104 m away). No EAMENA record within 500 m Second image: HEXAGON A015c of June 1974 shows the same ring.</description><Point><coordinates>35.6584,31.7618,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Karama Ruins 14</name><description>Status: Checked. stone ring on a plateau. Position: image, tile A017e (1 Dec 1974), window registered to the elevation model (155 blocks, 12 m) (error approximately 30 m). Round feature approximately 11 m across on a field plateau north of a gorge. APAAME photographs of 24 Sep 2017 show a ring of stones on a ploughed plateau near a gorge edge, with two small rectangular enclosures near it (Flickr list position 199 m away). No EAMENA record within 500 m HEXAGON A015c of June 1974 shows a faint light patch with one dark spot at the same place (weak). Second exposure: HEXAGON F017c (forward camera, 1 Dec 1974) shows the same round light feature with the same shadow and inner spot (block match 0.87). Checked on two exposures of the same day; June 1974 is weak.</description><Point><coordinates>35.6727,31.7689,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Karama Ruins 16</name><description>Status: Checked. round structure on a knoll. Position: image, tile A017e (1 Dec 1974), window registered to the elevation model (79 blocks, 10 m) (error approximately 30 m). Round light feature approximately 18 m across on a small flat-topped knoll above a scarp. APAAME photographs of 24 Sep 2017 show a ring on a flat-topped knoll above a scarp, and more rings on the plateau near it (Flickr list position 263 m away). No EAMENA record within 500 m Second image: HEXAGON F007d of 5 May 1978 shows the same knoll with a ring wall, clearer than in 1974.</description><Point><coordinates>35.6302,31.766,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>ʿAin Duk, head of the spring gardens</name><description>Status: Probable. spring (head of the irrigated plots). Position: images F016b (1 Dec 1974) and F006c (5 May 1978), each linked to a registered frame through the frame overlap (51 and 11 blocks) (error approximately 60 m). Trees and a small structure where the irrigated plots start, at the foot of the scarp; the two dates agree to 15 m. The water is not visible. EAMENA record: EAMENA-0117143 (3 m). The entry table uses this point from 11 Nov 2026; its old point (PEF sheet XVIII, georeferenced) is 415 m to the west-north-west on a bare slope.</description><Point><coordinates>35.4218,31.8963,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell el-Qos (published point)</name><description>Status: Not confirmed. tell in the built-up area of Jericho. Position: EAMENA-0117188; point shown on images F017b (1 Dec 1974) and F007c (5 May 1978) (error approximately 60 m). Open light ground approximately 60 m across on the north bank of Wadi Qelt in 1974; houses on a part of it in 1978. No mound shape can be read between the houses and trees. The entry table uses this point from 11 Nov 2026; its old point (PEF sheet XVIII, georeferenced) is 165 m to the north in an orchard with houses.</description><Point><coordinates>35.4648,31.8538,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Dome of the Rock (control for the Jerusalem window)</name><description>Status: Checked. control point. Position: published coordinate; the Jerusalem window of F017b is registered to the elevation model (141 blocks, 18 m with a height term) and then moved 48 m to put this point right (error approximately 15 m). With this one control, nine other landmarks with published coordinates (gates of the Old City, al-Aqsa, Holy Sepulchre, Church of All Nations) are at their places on the image, to approximately 30 m. The image of 5 May 1978 (F007c) is registered independently (30 blocks, 7 m with a height term; moved 19 m to this point): the same nine landmarks are at their places.</description><Point><coordinates>35.23528,31.77806,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell el-Ful, structure on the summit</name><description>Status: Checked. hilltop with a rectangular structure. Position: image, tile F017b (1 Dec 1974), Jerusalem window (error approximately 40 m). Terraced hill with a rectangular structure on the top. The entry-table point (Pleiades 749935552) is 8 m away. On the image of 5 May 1978 the point is approximately 35 m east of the centre of the large building on the summit.</description><Point><coordinates>35.2311,31.8235,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Machaerus, rectangle north-west of the citadel</name><description>Status: Checked. rectangular enclosure with rounded corners (probable Roman siege camp). Position: image, tile F018c (1 Dec 1974), Machaerus transform with height term (error approximately 30 m). Double line, approximately 65 m by 30 m, at the edge of a ridge above the wadi, 460 m west-north-west of the citadel summit. Also on the image of 25 June 1974 (aft camera, tile A016c): the same rectangle at the same place relative to the citadel. The camp letter of the published siege plan is not assigned. South of the scroll region.</description><Point><coordinates>35.6194,31.5695,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Machaerus, rectangle south-west of the citadel</name><description>Status: Checked. rectangular enclosure with rounded corners (probable Roman siege camp). Position: image, tile F018c (1 Dec 1974), Machaerus transform with height term (error approximately 30 m). Double line, approximately 44 m by 30 m, at the edge of a ridge above the wadi, 550 m west-south-west of the citadel summit. Also on the image of 25 June 1974 (aft camera, tile A016c): the same rectangle at the same place relative to the citadel. The camp letter of the published siege plan is not assigned. South of the scroll region.</description><Point><coordinates>35.6186,31.565,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mount Gerizim, octagonal church of Mary Theotokos</name><description>Status: Checked. church in a fortified enclosure. Position: coordinate of the CORPS database (ITM 225.95 / 678.48); identified on tile F014a (1 Dec 1974) and on a modern image (error approximately 30 m). Octagon with concentric rings inside a rectangular enclosure. Inner ring approximately 30 m; enclosure approximately 75 m west to east (database: church 30 by 37.4 m, enclosure 71 by 56 m). The registration to the elevation model puts it 166 m away (height effect at the summit); used as control point. Entry 57 place: table point 110 m north.</description><Point><coordinates>35.27331,32.19983,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mount Gerizim, monumental eastern staircase (plan part 34)</name><description>Status: Probable. staircase. Position: general plan of the precinct (Magen 2008, JSP 8, Fig. 14) fitted to a modern image of 29 Oct 2026 with five control points; position relative to the church (error approximately 15 m). Two or three parallel east-west lines, approximately 30 m long and 18 to 20 m apart, inside the plan outline (plan: approximately 21 by 31 m; report: up to 23 by 34 m). Single steps are not visible. Excavated after 1982; not visible in 1974. Entry 57 has 'the steps'; this is a position for a feature of that kind, not evidence for the entry.</description><Point><coordinates>35.27388,32.19982,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mount Gerizim, enclosure on the northern spur</name><description>Status: Probable. walled enclosure in a forest clearing. Position: image, tile F014a (1 Dec 1974), with the control point at the church (error approximately 80 m). Approximately 100 m across, 560 m north-north-east of the entry table point, above Nablus. Probable: Tell er-Ras. Not compared with the plans of Bull 1967 and 1968.</description><Point><coordinates>35.27564,32.20546,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Beth Shean, mound (Tell el-Husn), summit</name><description>Status: Checked. tell with excavation trenches. Position: image, tile b of frame D3C1209-200214F012 (1 Dec 1974), registered to the elevation model (local residual 18 m) (error approximately 40 m). Oval mound approximately 250 by 200 m above the bend of Nahal Harod; trenches on the summit. Also on tile d of frame D3C1208-400636F009 (25 Jun 1974), linked to the December image. Entry 58 place: table point on the mound, 60 m from the summit centre. Nahal Harod north of the mound checked with the site plan of NEAEHL vol. 5 p. 1624.</description><Point><coordinates>35.5029,32.50419,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Beth Shean, Roman theatre</name><description>Status: Checked. theatre. Position: image, tile b of frame D3C1209-200214F012 (1 Dec 1974) (error approximately 40 m). Semicircular structure 300 m south-south-west of the mound; agrees with the site plan of NEAEHL vol. 5 p. 1624. Also on the image of 25 Jun 1974.</description><Point><coordinates>35.50155,32.50135,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kh. Ibziq, oval mound with buildings</name><description>Status: Probable. mound with a wall or terrace line. Position: image, tile F013c (1 Dec 1974), registered to the elevation model (residual 40 m), no control point (error approximately 80 m). Approximately 170 m across, three or four standing buildings on its west side; a field of small walled cells 230 m east-south-east. 80 m from the entry table point (entry 59, possible). Which of the two survey ruins (Upper, Lower) this is, is not known.</description><Point><coordinates>35.39662,32.36846,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Beth Shean, ʿAin el-Melʿab (spring at the theatre)</name><description>Status: Possible. spring (position from a plan of 1882). Position: Plan of Beisan of the Survey of Western Palestine (Conder and Kitchener 1882, after p. 104; reproduced in Mazor and Najjar 2007, Fig. 1.1), placed relative to the theatre on tile b of frame D3C1209-200214F012 (error approximately 40 m). The plan of 1882 marks a spring ʿAin el-Melʿab at the east end of the theatre, with a stream to the north. On the images of 1 Dec 1974 and 25 Jun 1974, a dense group of trees is at this position; the spring is not visible. Entry 58 has 'the mouth of the spring'; this is a candidate position, not evidence for the entry. The plan also marks ʿAin el-Malhah 250 m south-west and ʿAin et-Tineh at the north-east bridge.</description><Point><coordinates>35.50241,32.50155,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Document></kml>